{
  "index_test": "whole-animal-in-vivo",
  "index_test_evidence": "Here we performed a simultaneous TG and PG assay (STPGA) to compare human response to a range of species (baboon, Rhesus macaque, swine, rat, rabbit and guinea pig) that are widely evaluated as animal models in hemostasis research and therapeutics development.",
  "decision": "include",
  "reason": "The study compares hemostasis parameters (thrombin and plasmin generation) between multiple animal species (baboon, Rhesus macaque, swine, rat, rabbit, guinea pig) and humans. It quantifies differences and similarities using statistical analysis of assay parameters (Peak Height, Production Rate), providing a quantitative measure of interspecies agreement/disagreement in biological response, which is relevant to the translation of animal model results to humans."
